Tom: A charity run? That sounds great. How far do you have to run?
Mia: Just five kilometres. You don''t have to be fast; you only have to finish.
Tom: And how does the run raise money?
Mia: Friends and family promise to donate some money for every runner who finishes.
Tom: That''s a clever idea. Can I still sign up?
Mia: Of course. You just fill in a form online and pay a small fee.
Tom: Brilliant. Let''s train together this week so we''re both ready.', 'Mia 邀请 Tom 下周日参加为儿童医院举办的慈善跑;只需跑五公里、跑完即可,不必跑得快;亲友为每位完赛者捐款;Tom 想报名,只需网上填表并交一点费用;两人决定本周一起训练。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is Mia going to do next Sunday?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Join a charity run.","Visit a hospital as a patient.","Move to a new house.","Watch a film at home."]},{"q":"How long is the run?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Fifteen kilometres.","Five kilometres.","Fifty kilometres.","Half a kilometre."]},{"q":"How does the run raise money?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["People donate money for each runner who finishes.","Runners pay to win a big prize.","The hospital sells the tickets.","Shops give away free clothes."]},{"q":"How can Tom sign up?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Phone the hospital director.","Fill in a form online and pay a small fee.","Send a letter by post.","Visit Mia''s house tonight."]},{"q":"What do they decide to do this week?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Buy new running shoes.","Cancel the whole plan.","Train together to get ready.","Rest at home every day."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U2', 'fltrp');
These shops sell second-hand clothes, books and toys that people no longer want.
Kind volunteers, not paid workers, run most of them.
The money from each sale goes to a good cause, such as fighting cancer or helping the homeless.
Shopping there is good for everyone, so next time you pass a charity shop, why not step inside?', '在英国许多商业街上你会看到慈善商店;这些店出售人们不再需要的二手衣物、书籍和玩具;大多由志愿者而非雇员经营;每笔收入都用于慈善事业,如抗癌或帮助无家可归者;在那里购物对大家都有好处,下次路过不妨进去看看。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What do charity shops mainly sell?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Brand-new cars.","Fresh food and drinks.","Tickets to concerts.","Second-hand clothes, books and toys."]},{"q":"Who runs most charity shops?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Volunteers, not paid workers.","Government officers.","Famous singers.","Hospital doctors."]},{"q":"Where does the money from sales go?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To the shop owners'' pockets.","To a good cause.","Back to the buyers.","To build more shops."]},{"q":"What is one good cause mentioned?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Building a sports stadium.","Buying expensive cars.","Fighting cancer or helping the homeless.","Holding music shows."]},{"q":"What does the speaker suggest doing?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Never visiting such shops.","Opening your own shop.","Asking for free clothes.","Stepping inside a charity shop next time."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required3', 'U2', 'fltrp');
Sarah: Hello. I''d like to become a volunteer. Could you tell me what work you have?
Clerk: Certainly. We need people to help teach children with disabilities at a riding centre.
Sarah: That sounds perfect. I love horses and I enjoy being with children.
Clerk: Wonderful. We''d like you to help out three times a week, if possible.
Sarah: That''s fine. What do I need to do to start?
Clerk: Just fill in a registration form. We''ll then send you a letter of confirmation.
Sarah: Thank you. Is there anything else I should know?
Clerk: We''ll also ask about any experience you have, but don''t worry, training is provided.', 'Sarah 打电话到志愿者中心,想做志愿者并询问有什么工作;中心需要人在马术中心帮忙教残障儿童;Sarah 喜欢马也喜欢和孩子相处;中心希望她每周帮三次;开始前需填登记表,中心会寄确认信;还会询问经验,但提供培训。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why is Sarah calling the centre?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["To become a volunteer.","To book a horse-riding holiday.","To complain about a service.","To sell some old toys."]},{"q":"What work does the centre need help with?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Cleaning the streets at night.","Teaching children with disabilities at a riding centre.","Driving a school bus.","Cooking in a restaurant."]},{"q":"How often does the centre want Sarah to help?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Once a month.","Every single day.","Three times a week.","Only at weekends."]},{"q":"What must Sarah do to start?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Pass a difficult exam.","Pay a large sum of money.","Buy her own horse.","Fill in a registration form."]},{"q":"What does the clerk say about experience?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["They will ask about it, but training is provided.","No experience is ever allowed.","Only experts may apply.","Experience is not needed because the job is easy."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U2', 'fltrp');
Making a difference does not always need money.
You can give your time, your skills, or simply your kindness.
Visit a lonely neighbour, plant a tree, or help a classmate who is behind.
Small actions, repeated by many people, can change a whole community.
So the right question is not ''Why should I help?'' but ''How can I help today?''', '你也许以为只有富人或名人才能帮助世界,其实不然;有所作为并不总需要金钱;你可以付出时间、技能,或仅仅一份善意;探望孤独的邻居、种一棵树,或帮助落后的同学;许多人的微小行动能改变整个社区;关键问题不是''我为什么要帮'',而是''我今天能怎么帮''。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"According to the speaker, who can make a difference?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only very rich people.","Anyone, not only rich or famous people.","Only famous stars.","Only adults with money."]},{"q":"What does making a difference NOT always need?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Kindness.","Time.","Money.","Skills."]},{"q":"What examples of small actions are given?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Buying an expensive car.","Travelling around the world.","Building a tall tower.","Visiting a neighbour or planting a tree."]},{"q":"What can small actions by many people do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Change a whole community.","Make everyone rich.","Stop all the rain.","End every school."]},{"q":"What does the speaker say is the right question?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["''Why should I bother?''","''How can I help today?''","''When will I be famous?''","''How much will I earn?''"]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required3', 'U2', 'fltrp');
Anna: I''d love to. What kind of books do they need?
Leo: Mostly storybooks and simple science books for younger children.
Anna: I have a whole box of old picture books at home, and they''re in good condition.
Leo: That''s wonderful. Could you bring them to school on Friday?
Anna: Sure. Should we clean them first?
Leo: Yes, please. We want every book to look nice for the children.
Anna: No problem. It feels great to give my old books a new home.', 'Leo 说班里在为一所乡村学校收集图书,问 Anna 是否帮忙;学校主要需要故事书和给低龄孩子的简单科普书;Anna 家有一整箱品相不错的旧绘本;Leo 请她周五带到学校;还要先把书擦干净;Anna 很乐意,觉得让旧书有个新归宿很好。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is Leo''s class collecting?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Money for a new gym.","Clothes for a shop.","Books for a village school.","Food for a party."]},{"q":"What kind of books are needed?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Heavy university textbooks.","Old newspapers only.","Foreign novels for adults.","Storybooks and simple science books."]},{"q":"What does Anna have at home?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A box of old picture books.","A pile of new toys.","Several school bags.","A set of paintbrushes."]},{"q":"What does Leo ask Anna to do before Friday?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Sell the books.","Clean the books.","Paint the books.","Throw away the books."]},{"q":"How does Anna feel about giving her books away?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Sad to lose them.","Worried about the cost.","Glad to give them a new home.","Angry with her class."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U2', 'fltrp');
When you ask volunteers, their answers are often surprising.
Some say that helping others makes them feel useful and happy.
Others enjoy learning new skills or making new friends.
A few simply want to thank the world for the good luck they have had.
Whatever the reason, one thing is clear: when you help someone else, you often help yourself as well.', '你是否想过,为什么这么多人愿意无偿付出空闲时间去帮助别人?问问志愿者,他们的回答常常出人意料:有人说助人让自己感到有用又快乐;有人喜欢学习新技能、结交新朋友;也有人只是想回报自己拥有的好运;无论原因如何,有一点很清楚:当你帮助别人时,你往往也帮助了自己。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What question does the speaker begin with?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["How much volunteers earn.","Where charity shops are.","When the run will start.","Why people volunteer for no pay."]},{"q":"What do some volunteers say helping others makes them feel?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Useful and happy.","Tired and bored.","Rich and famous.","Angry and sad."]},{"q":"What do other volunteers enjoy about it?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Getting a free holiday.","Learning new skills or making friends.","Winning big prizes.","Avoiding hard work."]},{"q":"Why do a few people volunteer?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["To become world leaders.","To sell their old things.","To thank the world for their good luck.","To escape from school."]},{"q":"What is the speaker''s main point?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Volunteering is a waste of time.","Only money can help people.","Nobody should ever volunteer.","Helping others often helps yourself too."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required3', 'U2', 'fltrp');

